    "summary": "High‑energy Mason’s Children jam and Pigpen organ showcase",
    "blurb": "Features a fiery Mason's Children jam, gritty solos on Cold Rain And Snow, and Pigpen’s organ‑driven Turn On Your Lovelight. Phil delivers bass “bombs” on Hard To Handle. The set is raw, high‑energy despite occasional tape distortion.",
    "review": "The International Speedway show on December 28, 1969 finds the Dead in full festival mode, charging through a tight one‑set program with unbridled enthusiasm. Jerry’s guitar roars on Mason's Children and cuts a gritty line on Cold Rain And Snow, while Phil’s bass drops thunderous “bombs” during Hard To Handle, driving the band forward. Pigpen steals the spotlight with his organ swagger on Turn On Your Lovelight and peppered banter that keeps the crowd hooked. Although the monitor‑mix soundboard tape runs hot at times—producing distortion and occasional pitch wobble—the recording captures the raw, live vibe that makes this late‑’69 performance a memorable snapshot of the early Dead. For fans who want the most immediate feel, the Cotsman monitor mix remains the go‑to source despite its flaws.",
